        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: оплачивать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "оплачивать (opláchivat) — \"to pay for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Фирма оплачивает мне обед. Fírma opláchivayet mne obéd. The firm pays for my lunch."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective оплатить (оплачу, оплатишь). It takes a direct object with no за: оплачивать (opláchivat) счёт."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "оплачивать (opláchivat) is built from о- and платить \"to pay\", on плата \"a payment\", the root that also gives зарплата."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
